id: pm-cragzs
title: "GH-711: update must support intentional unresolved parent references under strict governance"
description: "Add create/update parity for an explicit allow-missing-parent escape hatch so strict parent_reference policy can support forward-declared hierarchy construction without disabling validation globally. GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/711"
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,gh-711,governance,relationships
created_at: "2026-07-25T15:23:57.781Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T17:52:36.495Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "pm update accepts the same allow-missing-parent escape hatch as pm create, with one shared flag spelling and one shared contract entry rather than a second per-command implementation; using it under strict parent_reference governance records a validation warning instead of failing, matching create-side behaviour exactly; omitting it preserves today's strict fail-fast on an unresolved parent; forward-declared hierarchy construction (child created or re-parented before its parent exists) round-trips through create and update without disabling parent validation globally; a parity spec asserts create/update agreement for the flag, its warning payload, and its history record"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: low
confidence: high
